416:/// Compute the canonical form of `dest_root` for use in
417:/// `verify_contained` calls. If `dest_root` exists, this is just
418:/// `canonicalize(dest_root)`. If it doesn't yet (e.g. the receive
419:/// operation will create it), we walk to the deepest existing
420:/// ancestor and canonicalize that — that's the only frame of
421:/// reference symlinks could escape from at write time, since
422:/// new directories created under it inherit its canonical
423:/// identity.
