425:/// R46-F3: every receive site that joins a wire-supplied
426:/// relative path under a destination root must pair `safe_join`
427:/// (lexical) with `verify_contained` (canonical), and the
428:/// canonical root needs to be computed once at the entry point
429:/// of the operation rather than per-entry. This helper is the
430:/// single chokepoint that gives all five sites the same
431:/// "deepest-existing-ancestor canonicalize" semantics.
